  53: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  54:     """
  55:     Copy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.
  56: 
  57:     Input structure:
  58:     - The background is the dominant color.
  59:     - Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.
  60:     - Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.
  61: 
  62:     Rule:
  63:     - Clear the grid to background.
  64:     - For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.
  65:     - Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.
  66: 
  67:     Key insight:
  68:     - A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.
